The House of the Dragon TV show very  closely follows George R.R Martin's Fire  and Blood novel but there are still  differences between the show and the  book since there's not enough time in  this video to go through every change  that they've made I've gone and found  the 10 craziest differences between the  house of the Dragon TV show and the book  there will obviously be spoilers so  don't watch this video If you're not  fully caught up  [Music]  number 10 Laris Strong's murders in the  house of the Dragon TV series Lara  strong is shown to be the one to  instigate the great fire at harrenhal  that killed both Lord Lionel strong his  father and Sir Harwin strong his brother  he did so by setting three prisoners  free cutting out their tongue so they  couldn't speak about what lairs told  them to do and having them set fire to  his family's room at harrenhal in the  book however the fire was blamed on the  curse of harrenhal although maesters and  historians suspected other culprits for  the fire including Prince Damon  Targaryen Lord Corliss valerion King  viserys Targaryen and also Lara strong  this change makes a significant impact  on the story at large changing  everything we know about Laris and his  willingness to do whatever it takes to  climb his way up in westerosi society  although it's not explicitly shown that  he intended to have his family murdered  so the question arises did Laris kill  his father and brother number nine  Damon's first wife Damon targaryen's  first wife and the heir to runestone  Lady Raya Royce was shown to have been  killed or helped to die by Damon and  House of the Dragon when she fell from  her horse and Damon finished her off  with a rock it was shown that he had  come to runestone to claim his place as  the local Lord but in the book Fire and  Blood lady Royce was already the ruling  Lady of runestone and Damon was fighting  in the stepstones when she died so  instead of being killed by Damon it was  written that she died when she fell from  her horse while hunting in the veil he  later flew to runestone on his Dragon  character's when he heard of her death  to make his claim for the ruling seat at  runestone which he was denied the change  in story to demon killing his wife who  he called the bronze [ __ ] really shows  Demon's character and his distaste for  anyone not of Targaryen or Valyrian  ancestry number eight fact versus  fiction one of the most significant  differences between House of the dragon  and fire and blood is that the series is  shown as an official account of the  events leading up to the dance of the  Dragons while the book is a collection  of second-hand stories which may not be  entirely factual Author George R.R  Martin wrote Fire and Blood as an  in-world history book by archmaester  gildane who wrote the book long after  the events of the dance of the dragons  in this this history book gildane uses  several different sources to write the  stories including accounts from septon  Eustis Grand maester Monken and the  court fool mushroom so the team working  on House of the dragon have had to adapt  the stories from somewhat biased sources  which a lot of the time each provides a  differing account of what happened  number seven eamon's eye House of the  Dragon gave us an absolutely stunning  scene where Eamon first bonded with the  titanic-sized dragon vegar afterward  we're shown a scene where rhaenira's son  luceris cuts out eamon's left eye  leading to Allison calling for one of  lucerus's eyes in Revenge although Eamon  says losing an eye was worth gaining a  dragon this scene differs in the book  however as Bayland Reyna Targaryen  weren't present Luke only cut out  eamon's eye after calling him and Jace  strongs and it was actually his right  eye that got cut out not as left number  six Lena's death in house of the Dragon  were shown Lena valerion in labor and  the maesters tell Eamon that they're  unable to get the child to be born  naturally Lena overhearing this decides  she does not want to die in childbirth  and instead wants to die a dragon  Rider's death so she walked out to her  dragon vegar and commanded it to breathe  fire on her shouting dracaryus and the  dragon obliged burning her alive in Fire  and Blood however Lena did give birth to  a son but he only survived for an hour  Lena's Health soon began to deteriorate  and three days after the delivery she  left her bed to try to fly on vegar one  last time but collapsed and died on her  way there this retelling of Lena's death  gives a much more powerful story for her  character showing her as a proud Dragon  Rider with the blood of old valyria  pulsing through her veins quick plug if  you like what you're seeing hit that  subscribe button for more videos like  this now back to the video number five  rhaenyra and Allison most of the scenes  early on in the show where Rainier and  Alice spend time together as friends  never really happened in the book in  fact Rainier and Allison weren't ever  true friends as Allison was nine years  older than Rainier in Fire and Blood in  House of the Dragon however they're  depicted as great childhood friends  spending lots of time together in the  godswood and the fact that they were  close friends as children places even  more tension on their relationship when  Allison Mary's Ray near his father  viserys in the book though they really  don't even have a relationship until  Allison marries viserys before then they  likely knew of each other but hardly  spoke to one another I think this change  from the book was really great creating  scenes with a lot more drama and higher  Stakes at hand number 4. lenor's Death  In The House of the Dragon series we saw  rhaenyra and her husband Lenor valerion  at a point in their sham marriage where  Rainier wanted to move on to unite  herself with her Uncle Damon gross and  Lenor wanted to run away from his  problems with his lover sir Carl Corey  the series shows us how demon offered  Carl and Leonor the opportunity to run  away together across the narrow Sea by  staging a fight and faking leanor's  death they do so as opposed to the book  Fire and Blood where Carl actually kills  laner for money leaving Leonard's Dragon  sea smoke riderless this was likely done  in the show because without Damon giving  laner the option to run away he'd simply  be seen as a bloodthirsty murderer doing  whatever it takes to marry his niece  including paying someone to kill her  husband number three aegon's visions one  of the driving factors behind the first  season of House of the Dragon was  visiris's insistence upon passing on the  details of aegon the conqueror's vision  of the end of times where one Targaryen  would have to unite all the Realms of  men to fight against a great winter in  the darkness that comes with it a vision  he called A Song of Ice and Fire but it  was never actually mentioned in the book  and neither were any of the Targaryen  dreams besides Danish the dreamer's  vision about the Doom of valyria it was  aegon's dream of the great winter that  pushed him to conquer and unite the  Seven Kingdoms giving a much more  in-depth backstory as to the reasoning  for why aegon was so relentless in his  Conquest although it was never fully  mentioned in the book it was George RR  Martin's idea to include this plotline  about Visions so he could still tie it  in with the storylines and the books  later on number two vaman's death the  ninth episode of House of the Dragon  gave us the death of Lord cordless  valerian's brother vaman valerion when  he was beheaded by Daemon Targaryen and  the red keep when Corliss was injured in  a battle in the stepstones vaman made  the claim that he was the true heir to  driftmark because rhaenya and leaner's  children were bastards but he went a bit  too far calling Rainier is some  expletive terms and dismissing her claim  to the Iron Throne so viserys called for  his tongue and immediately Damon instead  cut his head in half saying he could  keep his tongue in the book Fire and  Blood however the events happened quite  differently instead of being injured in  battle Lord Corliss Valerian became sick  and the question of who might take his  place on the driftmark throne arose  rhaenyra urged for his son Luke to be  named as the heir to driftmark as her  firstborn son Jace would be heir to the  Iron Throne after her vehmond still in  driftmark stated that her children were  bastards and had no claim to driftmark  outraged by this Rainier had her husband  Damon fly to driftmark where he beheaded  vemond and brought the head back to  Rainier which she fed to her Dragon  Cyrax while I do think it would have  been cool to see Rainier and Damon use  their dragons a bit more feeding their  enemies heads to the beasts I understand  why this change was made probably for  budgetary reasons also without this  change we wouldn't have gotten the  amazing scene where the old and sickly  viserys arrives in the red keep like a  bat to stand up for his daughter and  grandsons number one rainys in the  dragon pit episode 9 of House of the  Dragon also gave us a really intense  scene where princess rhaenice the queen  that never was burst through the floor  of the Dragon pit on her Dragon melees  killing hundreds of civilians in King's  Landing before she comes face to face  with Queen Allison and the newly crowned  King aegon II she decides to fly away  rather than burn them to a crisp which  would have stopped all the mounting  tensions leading up to the impending  Civil War but none of this happened in  the book rhaenys didn't destroy the  dragon pit floor she didn't kill  hundreds of innocent people and she  never had the chance to burn Allison and  her children and one fell swoop in Fire  and Blood she was already back at  driftmark when aegon was crowned as king  at this point in time I think this might  be one of the biggest and one of the  most unnecessary changes made so far I  don't feel like it added much to  rhaenys's character because her actions  are just so contradictory on one hand  she's willing to kill hundreds of  civilians to get her Dragon but on the  other she's not willing to kill the  usurpus for the throne to put a stop to  the Civil War that will kill thousands  it just doesn't really make sense I get  that the writers wanted an epic  conclusion leading up to the season  finale but it feels like this scene  definitely could have been done  differently but I'd like to know what  you think which changes do you like the  most and the least drop your thoughts in  the comment section below also check out  the video on your screen for some more  of my content don't forget to like And  subscribe and thanks for watching Rocket  Riley  foreign

